Mutation
- [N8] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b1,n3,"v1 == \"Yes\""); source=i2:checking if the input is a "URN"; reason=The source specifies checking whether the input is exactly a 'URN', but the model alters this to an arbitrary 'v1 == Yes' condition.
- [N9] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b1,n4,"v1 == \"No\""); source=i4:If the input is a "URL", we simply continue with the process.; reason=The source explicitly conditions this path on the input being a 'URL', whereas the model distorts this check into 'v1 == No'.
- [N10] Node-level mutation: element=action(n6,"if URN perform ONS Resolving URN to a domain name") -> action(n7,"if URL continue process"); source=i7:and take the corresponding action.; reason=The source generically says to 'take the corresponding action'. The model violates strict fidelity by inventing and explicitly spelling out the specific steps (ONS Resolving / continue process), unpacking context rather than adhering to the written text.
